		{
			dependencies: ["7C84248F26B08F67"]
			description: [
				"With your Camera crafted and film in hand, you are ready to start shooting. Right-click with the Camera to enter the viewfinder mode, where you will see the world through the lens. The viewfinder interface shows your current settings and remaining film frames."
				""
				"To load film into your Camera, either sneak and right-click the Camera in your inventory to open the attachments menu, or right-click the Camera in a crafting grid with the film roll. The Camera accepts one film roll at a time, and you can see how many exposures remain through the viewfinder or item tooltip."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"While looking through the viewfinder, use the left mouse button to take a photo. The Camera has a default focal range of 18-55mm, which you can extend with lens attachments. Press the middle mouse button to open viewfinder controls where you can adjust zoom, shutter speed, and other settings."
				""
				"The Camera supports selfie mode by pressing F5 to switch to third-person front view. In selfie mode, the camera distance defaults to 1.75 blocks, giving you a comfortable framing distance for self-portraits and group photos."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The Camera supports four attachment slots that modify its behavior and capabilities. You can access the attachments menu by sneaking and right-clicking with the Camera or by right-clicking it in your inventory. Each slot accepts specific items that enhance your photography."
				""
				"The Flash slot accepts a Redstone Lamp to illuminate dark scenes when taking photographs. Once attached, the flash can be set to three modes: On (always fires), Off (never fires), or Auto (fires only when light level at the Camera position is below 8). The flash illuminates a small area in front of the Camera, helping capture clear images in caves, at night, or in dark builds."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The Lens slot accepts a Spyglass to extend your Camera's focal range. The default Camera offers an 18-55mm focal range suitable for standard photography. Attaching a Spyglass changes this to a 55-200mm telephoto range, allowing you to zoom in on distant subjects like faraway builds, wildlife, or landscapes without getting close."
				""
				"The Filter slot accepts any Glass Pane to apply color tints to your photographs. Using stained glass panes creates stylized images with that color cast, while clear glass panes have no effect."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Red, Green, and Blue filters are particularly useful for the advanced Chromatic printing process, allowing you to capture individual color channels for later combination. The Filter slot also accepts the Interplanar Projector for importing external images into the game as photographs."
			]
			id: "5461D49FEBD09FAC"
			rewards: [{
				id: "553FE0D8D0E6CDF4"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 100
			}]
			tasks: [{
				id: "1B30AD74AB1136F1"
				item: "exposure:camera"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: -2.5d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7C84248F26B08F67"]
			description: ["The classic Black and White Film produces timeless monochrome photographs with excellent contrast. Craft it using Iron Ingots, Iron Nuggets, Bone Meal, Gunpowder, and Dried Kelp. This film develops with just a Water Bottle, making it the most accessible option for beginners."]
			id: "1930CF6C6F3F3E28"
