		{
			dependencies: ["5461D49FEBD09FAC"]
			description: [
				"The Camera Stand transforms photography from handheld snapshots into a more controlled studio experience. This tripod-like entity holds your Camera in place, enables remote triggering, and unlocks group photo capabilities."
				""
				"Place the Camera Stand in the world, then right-click it while holding a Camera to mount your equipment. Once mounted, right-click the stand to enter control mode where you can aim the Camera and adjust settings. Sneak while interacting to access the Camera's attachment menu directly on the stand."
				""
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The Camera Stand has a working range of 100 blocks. If the owner moves beyond this range, the stand may malfunction and require a simple right-click interaction to repair. This range limitation ensures the Camera can properly render the scene from the player's loaded chunks."
				""
				"The Camera Stand supports a self-timer feature perfect for group photos and selfies without the handheld Camera. When the timer activates, it attracts the attention of nearby entities within a 16-block radius, causing mobs and animals to look toward the Camera for the perfect shot."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Camera Stands can be triggered with redstone signals, enabling automated photography setups. Connect redstone to the stand's position to trigger the shutter remotely. This opens possibilities for photo booths, security cameras, and creative automated capture systems."
				""
				"The stand can also ride in Boats and Minecarts, allowing mobile photography platforms. When placed in a rideable Minecart, you can create moving camera rigs for cinematic shots along rail systems."
			]
			id: "521AB787E3C90B6F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "37E0C7A551EE3155"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 100
